# GET /drain — step 2: drain the namespace inside ONE op.
#
# kv/list is windowed: at most `limit` keys per call, sorted after the
# `after` cursor, with `next` = the cursor for the following call ("" when
# the namespace is exhausted). Without repeat_until you would need a
# @goto loop — a full stage hop per page, with every sibling op at the
# target scope re-evaluated each time. With it, this op re-runs itself:
#
#   - `after = ._page.next` is re-resolved every pass against the view
#     (envelope + everything merged so far), so the cursor advances;
#   - passes merge with the scope-merge rules — `keys` (an array)
#     appends, `next` and `count` (scalars) take the last pass's value;
#   - the loop stops when `._page.next == ""` holds (done), at
#     repeat_max passes (max), on a pass error, on fuel, or on the op's
#     WITH timeout — and the scope sees ONE merged payload either way.
#
# Five seeded keys at limit 2 → three passes: [a,b] [c,d] [e].
# What happened is written to @runtime.repeat.drain = {passes, stop,
# elapsed_ms}; the responder at 300 copies it into the body.
WHEN @src == "http" && @web.req.url.path == "/drain"
  EXEC "txco://kv/list"
    WITH namespace = "drain-demo",
         limit = 2,
         after = ._page.next,
         into = "_page",
         repeat_until = ._page.next == "",
         repeat_max = 10
